1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,910
Your smartphone chimes brightly on payday morning with a fifteen million dong salary alert...

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:04,000
but between commercial bank vaults, not a single dong of physical currency actually moved across town.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,260
Because your company and you bank at the identical financial institution, funds never leave the building.

4
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:18,000
The bank simply edits two lines in its accounting ledger: corporate deposit debt decreases, while liability owed to you increases.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:25,370
The unspent portion of your salary resting in your checking account is classified as CASA — earning an illustrative 0.1 percent interest.

6
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:30,000
Across 500 colleagues, that creates an instant 2.5 billion dong low-cost funding pool.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:41,160
For that entire 2.5 billion funding pool, the bank pays barely two and a half million dong in annual interest.

8
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:51,000
If the institution raised that same capital through term deposits, it would pay 125 million dong.

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:59,000
In return for delivering your low-cost deposit pool to the bank, your company secures discounted corporate credit line margins, preferential loan rates, and extensive treasury fee waivers.

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,560
So where does your salary sleep tonight?

11
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:03,670
Inside the bank general ledger...

12
00:01:03,670 --> 00:01:10,000
and that dormant checking balance is quietly generating commercial profits for everyone except you.
